HARDWARE 

Hardware Components — Wildlife Anti-Poaching Drone System
1. Airframe
Primary platform: Small multirotor (recommended for MVP/Phase 1)
Secondary concept: Fixed-wing + multirotor hybrid fleet — fixed-wing for efficient large-area reconnaissance, multirotor for hover/inspect/detailed observation (noted as more complex due to differing launch/recovery needs)
Persistent-surveillance variant: Tethered UAV for selected high-risk zones (continuous power/data via tether; not suited for roaming patrol)

2. Sensing Payload
Sensor	Function
Thermal camera	Detects exposed human/animal heat signatures; effective at night/low light; cannot see through dense vegetation
RGB camera	Daytime visual confirmation, classification, evidence capture
Acoustic sensor array	Gunshot-impulse detection; multiple units enable source localization
LiDAR / depth camera	Optional; terrain/vegetation mapping and obstacle avoidance (not for seeing through foliage)
GNSS/GPS	Positioning and GPS-tagged detections/alerts

3. Flight & Navigation Electronics
Flight controller: Pixhawk-class
Firmware/autopilot: ArduPilot or PX4
Additional nav sensors: IMU (orientation/motion), barometer (altitude), obstacle sensors (local avoidance)
Companion computer: Raspberry Pi- or Jetson-class board (for onboard AI inference/processing)

4. Power System
Battery chemistry: LiPo (favored for power-to-weight ratio in multirotor prototypes)
Endurance target (illustrative, not guaranteed): ~25–35 min per sortie; example planning model: 30 min nominal − 8 min reserve = 22 min usable patrol time
Energy infrastructure:
Forward battery stations (solar panel → stationary battery bank → drone charging/swap)
Mobile drone base (vehicle-transported drones, batteries, charging gear)
Solar-powered ground station (preferred over onboard solar panels)
Tethered ground dock (continuous power/data delivery via cable)

5. Ground/Control Infrastructure
Central Wildlife Control Room
Range-level/strategic drone bases (example: 2 drones per Range)
Dashboard system displaying live drone position, map, detections, alerts, patrol sectors

Notes/Caveats stated in the source
No hardware spec is treated as final — battery life, coverage area, and detection range are called "illustrative planning calculations," not guaranteed specifications.
Actual coverage depends on real specs of the selected drone (flight time, speed, camera FOV, altitude, target size, vegetation, weather).
